### A delivery signed with the wrong key: 401 before any of the host's code runs — sent FIRST, so the job is still
### `scheduled` and a forged completion that got through would be visible
# @name Forged
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [401]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/hooks/technician-app
webhook-id: {{ForgedId}}
webhook-timestamp: {{MobileTimestamp}}
webhook-signature: {{ForgedSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{MobileBody}}

### The forged delivery changed nothing
# @name ReadAfterForged
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The app's signed "job completed": WO-7001 is only scheduled, so the host starts AND completes it in one unit
# @name Complete
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/hooks/technician-app
webhook-id: {{MobileId}}
webhook-timestamp: {{MobileTimestamp}}
webhook-signature: {{MobileSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{MobileBody}}

###
# @name ReadAfterComplete
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The minutes were recorded on the job's visit
# @name VisitAfterComplete
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/visits?work_order_id=eq.{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The app's retry of the very same delivery: acknowledged without running again
# @name CompleteAgain
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/hooks/technician-app
webhook-id: {{MobileId}}
webhook-timestamp: {{MobileTimestamp}}
webhook-signature: {{MobileSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{MobileBody}}

###
# @name ReadAfterReplay
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
